well developing at noon rapper travis  scott is pulling out of this weekend's  day in vegas festival the music festival  here in the valley he was on stage in  houston friday night when a crowd surge  at that festival killed at least eight  people lilia luciano reports  cell phone video shows a panicked  festival goer at friday night's asteroid  concert pleading for help from a camera  operator but the show would go on  authorities say when scott took the  stage at approximately 9 pm the crowd of  more than 50 000 rushed forward  people began passing out in the crush  video shows first responders treating  the injured but authorities say they  were overwhelmed  by the end of the night at least eight  people would die with more than a dozen  hospitalized in scores injured as the  crowd surge spun out of control  kayla jay was there and says she tried  to shield a man who had fallen to the  ground but she now fears he's among the  dead i just held his hand until like  until like he like he let go  roughly half an hour after the show  started it was declared a mass casualty  event later on scott stopped his set to  help someone in the crowd but started  again soon after his show didn't end  until about 10 10 pm almost 40 minutes  after the mass casualty event had been  declared  on saturday houston chief of police troy  finner defended the decision we have to  worry about riding riots it was a  cooperation and discussion between  promoters  my fire department the police department  scott posted this video on instagram the  next day saying he was unaware of the  severity of the situation in the crowd  i'm honestly just devastated and  i could never imagine anything like this  just  happening but some survivors say  authorities did not do enough like basil  bake he was at the festival with his  brother donish who was killed in the  crowd he got lost in the crew i looked  over my shoulder he was there once again  he did not deserve this he did not  deserve this he did not deserve this  okay both scott and the concert  promoters at live nation say they've  been cooperating with local authorities  and now police say their narcotics unit  became involved after a security guard  alleged that he was pricked on the neck  with a needle and had to be resuscitated  with narcan however at this point  there's no evidence to indicate that  that incident had anything to do or  triggered the deadly crowd surge  luciano cbs news houston
 

